      "summary": "The zero-diff bypass does not prove that the exact head has trusted reconciliation ancestry.",
      "findingsComplete": true,
      "blockingFindings": [
        {
          "id": "df-2d339cf66fed9a28146e",
          "title": "Zero-diff admission accepts untrusted or malformed ancestry",
          "details": "At head 0e2873d2f7b386ef1d689c63debdf9f744088845, admission requires only the PR's bot author, a release/reconcile branch prefix, base ancestry somewhere in the graph, identical trees, and an empty diff. The PR author does not prove who pushed the exact head to its same-repository branch. A collaborator can replace an engine-created branch with an arbitrary same-tree history containing the base as a non-first-parent ancestor, and the check will bypass every model round. The implementation also deliberately admits reachedBase=false/complete=false evidence and suppresses malformed bounded ancestry as boundedOut. Require deterministic exact-head provenance and an admissible reconciliation commit/parent structure; malformed or incomplete required ancestry evidence must block closed.",
          "path": ".github/scripts/run-darkfactory-autoreview.mjs",
          "line": 1308
        }
      ],
